{
 "_readme": "Periods, each with its terms (oldest first). A term is labelled from-to with overlapping years, because terms start in July, and covers the calendar years from..to-1. People without \"from\"/\"to\" serve the whole term; give \"from\" (a year, or \"Mon YYYY\") when someone joins mid-term and \"to\" when someone leaves. Each \"from\" becomes a row under the term. Roles containing \"Information Director\", \"DiSC\" or \"Anthology\" go to the Information Director column, \"Conference Coordinator\" to its own column, everything else to Other members. SIGMOD PC chairs (from 2020) come from programChairs.json. A source with \"when\" goes on that year's row if there is one, otherwise on the term row. A person with \"inline\": true is shown on the term row with their years instead of on a row of their own. A period may set \"issueLabel\" for the Term column heading. Terms with \"yearRows\": true (since 2013) have a row for every year, listing the PC chairs, PODS chair and TODS EiC of that year, and put everyone who did not serve the whole term, except Record editors, on the row of the year they started, with their years. \"column\": \"other\" puts a person in Other members whatever their role. \"noYears\": true hides a person's years on the page. \"showYears\": true shows the years even for someone who served the whole term. Since 1993 sources sit on the term row (at most four per term), except Hammer's 1999 one.",
